2. Pick the wake mechanism. OpenCode has no /loop; you drive the polling yourself. An event to watch (CI, a merge, a ref advancing) gets a blocking watcher command (`gh pr checks <number> --watch`, `gh run watch`) or a bash loop that sleeps and re-checks, with a long time-based heartbeat as fallback. No event gets a fixed-interval `sleep`-and-recheck sized to when the result is worth re-checking.
